    "text": "recall@k and MRR@10 are the cross-chunking comparison metrics (C1 against C2). nDCG@10 compares retrievers within one chunking: gain = share of gold units newly covered, ideal = greedy cover of the same chunking; cross-chunking pairs are therefore compared on recall@5 only and no cross-chunking nDCG interval exists. mean_retrieved_tokens_at_k gives the context size behind each k, counted with the e5 tokenizer over the full chunk text including the C2 header line (mean_tokens_C1/C2 in the corpus block count the chunk body only). The reranker reads at most max_length tokens of each (query, chunk) pair: truncation.<chunking>.reranker gives the share of reranked top-k pairs that lose their tail, next to the embedder table. The headline block names the configuration declared in advance, not the best one: see headline.best.note.",
